  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Scaler** `scalers/05-queue-backlog.yaml` &nbsp;\u00b7&nbsp; **Load** `loadgen/queue.yaml` (pushes 100 jobs) &nbsp;\u00b7&nbsp; **Expect** workers 0 \u2192 several (up to 10) \u2192 back to 0 once the queue is empty.\n\nReplicas = `ceil(backlog \u00f7 10)`. The workers are Redis consumers (`worker-d`); each takes ~2 s per job. The backlog is `redis_key_size{key=\"jobs\"}` from the redis_exporter sidecar. The workers expose no metrics of their own, so per-worker numbers here are pod CPU/memory, and throughput is estimated from how fast the backlog falls."
      },
      "transparent": true,
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      }
